course: dictionary
lesson: 7762
title: Purple, a colour with a royal past
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Purple is a colour you get by mixing red and blue, like grapes, plums and violets. It can be an adjective, as in a purple scarf, or a noun, as in the colour purple. Adjectives can change too: purple, purpler, purplest.
explain: Context helps you use the word. «Reds, oranges and yellows are called warm colours and blues, greens and purples cool colours, because of the feelings people link with them.» Here purples sits in a group with blues and greens, so it is a colour in the cool group.
explain: Purple has a royal past. Long ago it was a colour worn by kings and queens, because the dye used to make it was very costly. So when you read about purple robes in a story, think about wealth and power.
fact: Purple is a colour made by mixing red and blue.
fact: Purple can be an adjective (a purple scarf) or a noun (the colour purple).
fact: The comparative and superlative forms are purpler and purplest.
fact: Purple was once worn by kings and queens, because its dye was very costly.
fact: Purple is one of the cool colours, along with blue and green.
exercise: Which two colours do you mix to make purple? | Orange and pink | *Red and blue | Green and yellow | Black and white
exercise: «A little lemon juice brings the purple back» in the blueberry sentence. What brings the purple back? | Baking soda | Green colour | *Lemon juice | Too much batter
exercise: Long ago, purple was worn by kings and queens. Why was it so special? | It was the cheapest dye | *Its dye was very costly | It was the only colour that existed | Kings were colour blind
test: «Reds, oranges and yellows are called warm colours and blues, greens and purples cool colours.» What are purples called in this sentence? | Dark colours | Bright colours | Warm colours | *Cool colours
test: The phrase «purple with rage» is used to describe someone. What does it suggest? | Very tidy | Very sleepy | *Very angry | Very cold
exam: Which two colours mixed together make purple? | Yellow and green | *Red and blue | Black and white | Orange and pink
